Stop different paints sharing one cached pixmap

drawLightBevel() keys the pixmap of a bevel on the widget kind, the mask,
the round mode, the size, the state, the fill and the radius. The paint
inside the pixmap also reads the widget. drawEtch() takes a white line for
the groove of a scroll bar. It takes a shade of the parent background for
every other widget. The kind WIDGET_SLIDER_TROUGH covers the groove of a
slider and the groove of a scroll bar. The two grooves therefore share one
key, and the second groove takes the pixmap of the first. The scroll bar
groove then loses its own etch colour on 449 pixels. The key now holds the
etch colour of the widget. It also holds the checkable flag, because the
glow of a pressed button reads that flag.

createKey() packs the appearance into five bits. EAppearance holds forty
values, so APPEARANCE_DARK_INVERTED shares a key with custom gradient one.
Seven further pairs up to APPEARANCE_LV_AGUA share a key as well. The
appearance field now holds six bits, and the cache type moves one bit up.
The colour of the same key also lost the top bit of its alpha channel,
because the shift ran in the width of QRgb. The code now widens the colour
before the shift. The key holds 58 bits of the 64 bits of the cache.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 1 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

